{%- doc -%}
  Renders the mobile drawer's promo-tile slider for a top-level menu item whose matched mega
  menu panel has `_mega-menu-promo` tiles nested under it (grid-style panels; a tabbed panel, or
  a top-level item with no matched panel at all, has none and this renders nothing). Reuses
  Horizon's stock featured-content strip shell so it sits, scrolls, and staggers-in exactly like
  the built-in collection/product strip (snippets/header-drawer.liquid), one
  `<li class="...featured-content-list-item--card">` per tile - see the CSS comment in
  assets/custom.css ("Mobile drawer: thumbnails & promo slider") for how a single
  `<li>`-wrapped `_mega-menu-promo` block serves both the desktop grid and this strip, and for
  how a tile with neither an image nor a caption is hidden rather than skipped here (this
  snippet has no per-tile data of its own to test - see blocks/_mega-menu-promo.liquid).

  Called by blocks/_mega-menu-panel.liquid only when it is rendering for the drawer
  (`drawer: true`, set by blocks/_header-menu.liquid's mobile variant).

  @param {string} promo_tiles - The captured `content_for 'blocks'` output of the matched
    panel's own nested `_mega-menu-promo` blocks (blank when the panel has none).

  @example
  {% render 'mega-menu-drawer-promos', promo_tiles: promo_tiles %}
{%- enddoc -%}

{% if promo_tiles != blank %}
  <div class="menu-drawer__featured-content menu-drawer__featured-content--childlist">
    <ul class="menu-drawer__featured-content-list list-unstyled">
      {{ promo_tiles }}
    </ul>
  </div>
{% endif %}
